{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"jq -r '.claims | to_entries[] | select(.key>=14) | \\\"\\\\(.key): \\\\(.value.claim)\\\\n  ids=\\\\(.value.source_ids|tojson) locations=\\\\(.value.source_locations//[]|tojson)\\\"' claims_grounding.json; jq 'keys' validation_report.json; jq '.summary' scientific-evidence/verification-report.json; jq '.final_evaluation.evaluation_evidence | keys' paper_data.json; jq 'keys' source_evidence/resources/final/manifest.json\"","aggregated_output":"14: Budgets 1,2,4,8 use nested prefixes; seeds 6841,8089,9011; history/test sizes 94/32 except final family split 93/33; six primary condition/seed averages have equal weight.\n  ids=[\"final.evidence.episodes\"] locations=[\"source_evidence/resources/final/plan.json:1\",\"source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:970\"]\n15: Aggregate MAE 0.040807843083862115, RMSE 0.06432104648676243, strongest aggregate baseline 0.045249969215420516, gain 0.004442126131558401, relative reduction 9.816860008%.\n  ids=[\"final.metric.mae\",\"final.metric.rmse\",\"final.metric.baseline_mae\",\"final.metric.delta_best_baseline\"] locations=[\"derived_results.json:1\"]\n16: All six estimators and both holdouts in Table 1, the complete budget table, and seed table reproduce retained episode arrays; the studied configuration has lower aggregate MAE in each holdout than every reference.\n  ids=[\"final.evidence.episodes\"] locations=[\"derived_results.json:1\",\"tables/main_comparison.tex:1\",\"tables/budget_details.tex:1\",\"tables/seed_details.tex:1\"]\n17: Studied MAE model/family=0.038312665669/0.043303020499 versus linear ridge 0.045116500008/0.045383438423; partitions differ, so no causal effect of family membership is inferred.\n  ids=[\"final.evidence.episodes\"] locations=[\"derived_results.json:1\"]\n18: Studied seed MAEs 0.038496586319,0.041126033629,0.042800909303 (sample SD 0.002169731091); linear-ridge seed MAEs 0.041657905965,0.045940218194,0.048151783488. Seeds share source data.\n  ids=[\"final.evidence.episodes\"] locations=[\"derived_results.json:1\"]\n19: Primary budget MAEs 0.045233341978,0.042208509062,0.039639061083,0.036150460213 decrease over k=1,2,4,8. Each holdout seed-mean curve decreases, without per-model monotonicity or sufficient-budget claims.\n  ids=[\"final.metric.mae_k1\",\"final.metric.mae_k2\",\"final.metric.mae_k4\",\"final.metric.mae_k8\",\"final.evidence.episodes\"] locations=[\"derived_results.json:1\"]\n20: At eight queries studied model/family errors are 0.034476748972/0.037824171454, versus ridge 0.039273276354/0.039840694780.\n  ids=[\"final.evidence.episodes\"] locations=[\"derived_results.json:1\"]\n21: Paired component resampling uses 400 draws and RNG 424242; quantiles .005/.995 for each of five baselines precede separate minima of lower and upper bounds. These are not a conventional single-comparator interval.\n  ids=[\"final.evidence.episodes\",\"final.metric.gain_ci_low\",\"final.metric.gain_ci_high\"] locations=[\"source_evidence/evaluate_final.py:999\",\"derived_results.json:1\"]\n22: Reported bound minima [0.0021032442082077377,0.009199712663056218] are reconstructed exactly; all baseline-specific intervals in the supplement come from the same retained paired arrays.\n  ids=[\"final.metric.gain_ci_low\",\"final.metric.gain_ci_high\",\"final.evidence.episodes\"] locations=[\"derived_results.json:1\"]\n23: Matched model-holdout intact MAE 0.038312665669 rises to 0.064367113099 under constant history and 0.068569520893 under column shifts; shifted column mean is 0.064367113099 and variance low-rank 0.070913935972. The method loses to column mean under shifts.\n  ids=[\"final.metric.constant_control_mae\",\"final.metric.permuted_control_mae\",\"final.evidence.episodes\"] locations=[\"derived_results.json:1\"]\n24: Constant-history column means and all centered historical linear references equal the studied sealed-target MAE; controls do not isolate any component.\n  id