{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"nl -ba source_evidence/selected/src/program.py | sed -n '1,197p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t\"\"\"CPU score-matrix prediction starter; only handle(request) is public.\n     2\t\n     3\tAll requests/responses are finite JSON objects. Additional response keys are forbidden.\n     4\tAll indices are zero-based, episode-local and opaque; no filenames or model IDs are used.\n     5\treset accepts ANY nonnegative integer seed and returns exactly {\"ok\": true}; it clears\n     6\tall state. Seeds initialize randomness, never choose a workload or evaluation plane.\n     7\t\n     8\tHistory upload (one per episode): upload_start fields shape=[M,N], dtype=\"float64\",\n     9\tbyteorder=\"little\", mask_dtype=\"uint8\", encoding=\"base64\", layout=\"values_then_mask\",\n    10\tnbytes=9*M*N, chunks=C. Bounds: 1<=M,N<=4096, 1<=C<=64, <=256 MiB logical data.\n    11\tReturns {\"ok\": true}. upload_chunk fields index (sequential 0..C-1) and data (base64\n    12\tstring, <=4 MiB decoded). Returns {\"ok\": true}. upload_commit has no other fields,\n    13\treturns {\"ok\": true}. Bytes are contiguous little-endian float64 [M,N] values then\n    14\tuint8 [M,N] observed mask, row major. Missing entries are zero with mask=0. Scores\n    15\thave already been normalized by public metric ranges to [0,1]. Buffers are private\n    16\tmemory, never shared files. At most one upload is live; outstanding transfer <=512 MiB.\n    17\t\n    18\tfit fields rank (positive integer <=16), sweeps (positive integer <=50), ridge\n    19\t(positive float). Returns {\"ok\": true}. These are requested settings, not scientific\n    20\tevidence of internal computation. Training uses history only. Fit/preprocessing must\n    21\tremain immutable until reset; no observations from new models may enter history.\n    22\t\n    23\tbegin fields trajectory (nonnegative int), queryable (distinct integer indices in\n    24\t0..N-1, at least eight), budget=8. Returns {\"ok\": true}. Clears only the current\n    25\tnew-model observations, never fitted history. select has no other fields; returns\n    26\texactly {\"index\": int}, an available not-yet-selected queryable index. observe fields\n    27\tindex (the most recently selected index) and value (finite [0,1] score); returns\n    28\t{\"ok\": true}. Only that score is authorized feedback. select/observe repeats eight\n    29\ttimes; predict is called after 1,2,4,8 observations and returns exactly\n    30\t{\"predictions\": [N finite floats in [0,1]]}. Predictions cover ALL N columns, including\n    31\tunobserved ones; target membership and masks are never disclosed. Predict must not\n    32\tconsume future observations. A new begin discards the preceding trajectory state.\n    33\t\n    34\tThe same operations/settings apply in reduced smoke and all production workloads.\n    35\tEvaluator-owned constant-history, independent-column permutation, constant/copy\n    36\tbaselines, and reset replay test this actual implementation under matched budgets.\n    37\tControls have no required direction of error change; null findings are legitimate.\n    38\tNo state flags, self-reported metrics, file outputs or undocumented response keys.\n    39\tNo adaptivity restriction: selection may be nonadaptive; inference uses observations.\n    40\tEach complete JSON message must be strictly below 64 MiB (chunks target below 8 MiB).\n    41\t\"\"\"\n    42\timport base64\n    43\timport math\n    44\t\n    45\timport numpy as np\n    46\t\n    47\t\n    48\t_state = {}\n    49\t\n    50\t\n    51\tdef _fit_residual_base(values, mask, rank, ridge, sweeps, rng):\n    52\t    rank = min(rank, *values.shape)\n    53\t    counts = mask.sum(axis=0)\n    54\t    means = np.divide((values * mask).sum(axis=0), counts,\n    55\t                      out=np.full(values.shape[1], 0.5), where=counts > 0)\n    56\t    centered = values - means\n    57\t    factors = rng.normal(0, .1, size=(values.shape[1], rank))\n    58\t    latent = np.zeros((values.shape[0], rank))\n    59\t    identity = ridge * np.eye(rank)\n    60\t    for sweep in range(sweeps):\n    61\t        for row in range(values.shape[0]):\n    62\t            design = factors[mask[row]]\n    63\t            latent[row] = np.linalg.solve(identity + design.T @ design,\n    64\t                                          design.T @ centered[row, mask[row]])\n    65\t        for column in range(values.shape[1]):\n    66\t            design = latent[mask[:, column]]\n    67\t            factors[column] = np.linalg.solve(identity + design.T @ design,\n    68\t                                              design.T @ centered[mask[:, column], column])\n    69\t    variance = np.divide((centered * centered * mask).sum(axis=0), counts,\n    70\t                         out=np.zeros(values.shape[1]), where=counts > 0)\n    71\t    return dict(means=means, factors=factors, ridge=ridge,\n    72\t                scales=np.maximum(np.sqrt(variance), 0.025))\n    73\t\n    74\t\n    75\tdef _condition_base(model, selected_indices, observed_scores):\n    76\t    factors, means = model['factors'], model['means']\n    77\t    design = factors[selected_indices]\n    78\t    latent = np.linalg.solve(model['ridge'] * np.eye(factors.shape[1]) + design.T @ design,\n    79\t                             design.T @ (np.asarray(observed_scores) - means[selected_indices]))\n    80\t    return np.clip(means + factors @ latent, 0, 1)\n    81\t\n    82\t\n    83\tdef _policy_index(model, selected_indices, available):\n    84\t    factors = model['factors']\n    85\t    covariance = np.linalg.inv(model['ridge'] * np.eye(factors.shape[1])\n    86\t                               + factors[selected_indices].T @ factors[selected_indices])\n    87\t    cross = factors @ covariance @ factors[available].T\n    88\t    denominator = 1 + np.sum((factors[available] @ covariance) * factors[available], axis=1)\n    89\t    gains = np.sum(cross * cross, axis=0) / denominator\n    90\t    return int(available[int(np.argmax(gains))])\n    91\t\n    92\t\n    93\tdef _donor_predictions(model, donor_scores, selected_indices):\n    94\t    predictions = np.broadcast_to(model['means'], donor_scores.shape).copy()\n    95\t    anchor_scores = donor_scores[:, selected_indices]\n    96\t    anchor_mask = np.isfinite(anchor_scores)\n    97\t    patterns, pattern_ids = np.unique(anchor_mask, axis=0, return_inverse=True)\n    98\t    for pattern_index, pattern in enumerate(patterns):\n    99\t        donor_indices = np.flatnonzero(pattern_ids == pattern_index)\n   100\t        if not pattern.any():\n   101\t            continue\n   102\t        anchors = np.asarray(selected_indices, dtype=int)[pattern]\n   103\t        design = model['factors'][anchors]\n   104\t        responses = anchor_scores[donor_indices][:, pattern] - model['means'][anchors]\n   105\t        latent = np.linalg.solve(model['ridge'] * np.eye(design.shape[1]) + design.T @ design,\n   106\t                                 design.T @ responses.T)\n   107\t        predictions[donor_indices] += latent.T @ model['factors'].T\n   108\t    return np.clip(predictions, 0, 1)\n   109\t\n   110\t\n   111\tdef _build_residual_bank(values, mask, pool_rows, inner_validation_rows,\n   112\t                         rank, ridge, sweeps, rng):\n   113\t    \"\"\"Every donor is excluded from its fit, including within nested validation.\"\"\"\n   114\t    donor_pool = rng.permutation(pool_rows)[:128]\n   115\t    folds = []\n   116\t    for donor_rows in np.array_split(donor_pool, 2):\n   117\t        fit_rows = np.setdiff1d(pool_rows, donor_rows)\n   118\t        assert np.intersect1d(inner_validation_rows, fit_rows).size == 0\n   119\t        assert np.intersect1d(inner_validation_rows, donor_rows).size == 0\n   120\t        assert np.intersect1d(fit_rows, donor_rows).size == 0\n   121\t        if donor_rows.size == 0 or fit_rows.size == 0:\n   122\t            continue\n   123\t        model = _fit_residual_base(values[fit_rows], mask[fit_rows], rank, ridge, sweeps, rng)\n   124\t        donor_scores = np.where(mask[donor_rows], values[donor_rows], np.nan)\n   125\t        folds.append(dict(model=model, scores=donor_scores))\n   126\t    if not folds:\n   127\t        return None\n   128\t    return dict(folds=folds, scores=np.concatenate([fold['scores'] for fold in folds]), cache={})\n   129\t\n   130\t\n   131\tdef _bank_residuals(bank, selected_indices):\n   132\t    key = tuple(selected_indices)\n   133\t    if key not in bank['cache']:\n   134\t        donor_target_scores = bank['scores']\n   135\t        donor_base_predictions = np.concatenate([\n   136\t            _donor_predictions(fold['model'], fold['scores'], selected_indices)\n   137\t            for fold in bank['folds']])\n   138\t        donor_residuals = donor_target_scores - donor_base_predictions\n   139\t        usable_donors = np.isfinite(donor_target_scores) & np.isfinite(donor_base_predictions)\n   140\t        donor_residuals[~usable_donors] = np.nan\n   141\t        if len(bank['cache']) >= 8:\n   142\t            del bank['cache'][next(iter(bank['cache']))]\n   143\t        bank['cache'][key] = donor_residuals\n   144\t    return bank['cache'][key]\n   145\t\n   146\t\n   147\tdef _profile_weights(donor_anchor_scores, observed_anchor_scores, anchor_scales,\n   148\t                      selected_indices, bandwidth):\n   149\t    common_mask = np.isfinite(donor_anchor_scores) & np.isfinite(observed_anchor_scores)[None, :]\n   150\t    overlap_count = common_mask.sum(axis=1)\n   151\t    differences = np.where(common_mask, donor_anchor_scores - observed_anchor_scores[None, :], 0.0)\n   152\t    squared_distance = np.sum((differences / anchor_scales) ** 2, axis=1)\n   153\t    squared_distance /= np.maximum(overlap_count, 1)\n   154\t    neighbor_weights = np.exp(-0.5 * squared_distance / bandwidth ** 2)\n   155\t    neighbor_weights *= overlap_count / max(len(selected_indices), 1)\n   156\t    neighbor_weights[overlap_count == 0] = 0.0\n   157\t    return neighbor_weights\n   158\t\n   159\t\n   160\tdef _bank_weights(bank, selected_indices, observed_anchor_scores, bandwidth):\n   161\t    return np.concatenate([\n   162\t        _profile_weights(fold['scores'][:, selected_indices], observed_anchor_scores,\n   163\t                         fold['model']['scales'][selected_indices], selected_indices, bandwidth)\n   164\t        for fold in bank['folds']])\n   165\t\n   166\t\n   167\tdef _weighted_median(residuals, weights):\n   168\t    order = np.argsort(residuals, kind='stable')\n   169\t    sorted_residuals, sorted_weights = residuals[order], weights[order]\n   170\t    median_index = np.searchsorted(np.cumsum(sorted_weights), 0.5 * sorted_weights.sum(), side=\"left\")\n   171\t    return sorted_residuals[min(median_index, len(sorted_residuals) - 1)]\n   172\t\n   173\t\n   174\tdef _correct_target(base_prediction, residuals, target_weights, blend_strength, shrinkage_strength):\n   175\t    weight_floor = 1e-12\n   176\t    if target_weights.sum() <= weight_floor: return base_prediction\n   177\t    effective_neighbors = target_weights.sum() ** 2 / max(np.dot(target_weights, target_weights), weight_floor)\n   178\t    residual_correction = _weighted_median(residuals, target_weights)\n   179\t    correction_weight = blend_strength * effective_neighbors / (effective_neighbors + shrinkage_strength)\n   180\t    prediction = base_prediction + correction_weight * residual_correction\n   181\t    return prediction\n   182\t\n   183\t\n   184\tdef _residual_summaries(donor_residuals, neighbor_weights):\n   185\t    columns = donor_residuals.shape[1]\n   186\t    medians, effective_counts = np.zeros(columns), np.zeros(columns)\n   187\t    for target in range(columns):\n   188\t        usable = np.isfinite(donor_residuals[:, target]) & (neighbor_weights > 0)\n   189\t        target_weights = neighbor_weights[usable]\n   190\t        weight_sum = target_weights.sum()\n   191\t        if weight_sum <= 1e-12:\n   192\t            continue\n   193\t        medians[target] = _weighted_median(donor_residuals[usable, target], target_weights)\n   194\t        effective_counts[target] = weight_sum ** 2 / max(np.dot(target_weights, target_weights), 1e-12)\n   195\t    return medians, effective_counts\n   196\t\n   197\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
