{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"jq '{totals,idea_titles,ablation_studies,evidence_sources, paper_profile}' paper_data.json | head -150; jq 'keys' derived_results.json; sed -n '1,180p' build_paper_artifacts.py; cat README.md\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"totals\": {\n    \"attempts\": 3,\n    \"correct_programs\": 2,\n    \"evaluated_programs\": 2,\n    \"ideas\": 3\n  },\n  \"idea_titles\": [\n    \"Overlap-Aware Transfer Design\",\n    \"Cross-Fitted Local Residual Medians\",\n    \"Support-Calibrated Residual Transport\"\n  ],\n  \"ablation_studies\": [],\n  \"evidence_sources\": {\n    \"ablations\": {\n      \"path\": \"work/results/r03/codex/20261117_111425/ablations\",\n      \"status\": \"missing\"\n    },\n    \"investigation\": {\n      \"path\": \"work/results/r03/codex/20261117_111425/investigation\",\n      \"status\": \"included\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"paper_profile\": \"standalone\"\n}\n[\n  \"baseline_gain_bounds\",\n  \"cases\",\n  \"changing_target_mae\",\n  \"methods\",\n  \"primary_mean\",\n  \"primary_seed\",\n  \"primary_seed_sd\",\n  \"relative_reduction\",\n  \"seeds\"\n]\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport matplotlib\nmatplotlib.use('Agg')\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nimport numpy as np\n\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nMETHODS = ['Column mean', 'Query mean', 'Random low-rank', 'Variance low-rank', 'Linear ridge', 'Residual transfer']\nCOLORS = ['#888888', '#bb9944', '#8064a2', '#d48232', '#408c87', '#2464a6']\n\n\ndef provenance(path, kind='figure'):\n    payload = dict(schema_name='scientific-evidence.artifact-manifest',\n                   artifact=dict(path=str(path), kind=kind, sha256=hashlib.sha256(path.read_bytes()).hexdigest()),\n                   derived_from=['@evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes]]', '@evidence[[build_paper_artifacts.py]]'],\n                   generated_by=dict(script_path='build_paper_artifacts.py', command=['python', 'build_paper_artifacts.py']))\n    Path(str(path) + '.prov.json').write_text(json.dumps(payload, indent=2))\n\n\ndef save_plot(figure, stem):\n    for extension in ['pdf', 'png']:\n        path = ROOT / 'figures' / (stem + '.' + extension)\n        figure.savefig(path, dpi=600, facecolor='white')\n        provenance(path.relative_to(ROOT))\n    plt.close(figure)\n\n\ndef main():\n    \"\"\"@evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes]]\n    @evidence[[source_evidence/evaluate_final.py#L970-L1045]]\n    \"\"\"\n    payload = json.loads((ROOT / 'paper_data.json').read_text())\n    final = payload['final_evaluation']\n    episodes = final['evaluation_evidence']['episodes']\n    seeds = [episode['seed'] for episode in episodes]\n    arrays = {}\n    for case in ['A', 'B', 'C', 'D']:\n        arrays[case] = []\n        for episode in episodes:\n            condition = episode['solution']['cases'][case]\n            baselines = np.asarray(condition['baseline_mae_by_method_row_checkpoint'])\n            studied = np.asarray(condition['mae_by_row_checkpoint'])[None, :, :]\n            arrays[case].append(np.concatenate([baselines, studied], axis=0).mean(axis=1))\n        arrays[case] = np.asarray(arrays[case])\n    primary_seed = (arrays['A'].mean(axis=2) + arrays['B'].mean(axis=2)) / 2\n    primary = primary_seed.mean(axis=0)\n    assert np.isclose(primary[-1], final['metrics']['mae'], atol=1e-14)\n    assert np.isclose(primary[:-1].min(), final['metrics']['baseline_mae'], atol=1e-14)\n    budget = (arrays['A'][:, -1].mean(axis=0) + arrays['B'][:, -1].mean(axis=0)) / 2\n    for index, count in enumerate([1, 2, 4, 8]):\n        assert np.isclose(budget[index], final['metrics']['mae_k' + str(count)], atol=1e-14)\n    summary = dict(seeds=seeds, methods=METHODS, primary_mean=primary.tolist(),\n                   primary_seed=primary_seed.tolist(), primary_seed_sd=primary_seed.std(axis=0, ddof=1).tolist(),\n                   cases={case:dict(seed_budget=values.tolist(), mean_budget=values.mean(axis=0).tolist(), mean=values.mean(axis=(0, 2)).tolist(), seed_sd=values.mean(axis=2).std(axis=0, ddof=1).tolist()) for case, values in arrays.items()},\n                   relative_reduction=float((primary[:-1].min() - primary[-1]) / primary[:-1].min()),\n                   changing_target_mae={case:float(np.mean([np.asarray(episode['solution']['cases'][case]['all_unqueried_mae_by_row_checkpoint']).mean() for episode in episodes])) for case in arrays})\n    gain_intervals = resample_bounds(episodes)\n    summary['baseline_gain_bounds'] = gain_intervals.tolist()\n    assert np.isclose(gain_intervals[0].min(), final['metrics']['gain_ci_low'])\n    assert np.isclose(gain_intervals[1].min(), final['metrics']['gain_ci_high'])\n    (ROOT / 'derived_results.json').write_text(json.dumps(summary, indent=2))\n    provenance(Path('derived_results.json'), 'derived')\n    create_tables(summary)\n    plt.rcParams.update({'font.size': 9, 'axes.labelsize': 9, 'axes.titlesize': 10, 'legend.fontsize': 9, 'xtick.labelsize': 9, 'ytick.labelsize': 9, 'pdf.fonttype': 42, 'axes.spines.top': False, 'axes.spines.right': False})\n    figure, axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(5.5, 2.65), sharey=True)\n    series = [5, 2, 3, 4]\n    for axis, case, title in zip(axes, ['A', 'B'], ['(a) Model holdout', '(b) Family holdout']):\n        for method in series:\n            mean = arrays[case][:, method].mean(axis=0)\n            deviation = arrays[case][:, method].std(axis=0, ddof=1)\n            axis.errorbar(range(4), mean, yerr=deviation, color=COLORS[method], marker='o', markersize=3.5, capsize=2, linewidth=1.4, label=METHODS[method])\n        axis.set(xticks=range(4), xticklabels=['1', '2', '4', '8'], xlabel='Queried columns, k', title=title, ylim=(0.025, 0.067))\n        axis.grid(axis='y', alpha=.16)\n    axes[0].set_ylabel('Sealed-target MAE')\n    handles, labels = axes[0].get_legend_handles_labels()\n    figure.legend(handles, labels, loc='lower center', ncol=2, frameon=False, columnspacing=1.1)\n    figure.subplots_adjust(left=.12, right=.98, bottom=.37, top=.87, wspace=.12)\n    save_plot(figure, 'budget_comparison')\n    figure, axis = plt.subplots(figsize=(4.95, 1.95))\n    for offset, method in zip([-.12, 0, .12], [5, 0, 3]):\n        means = [arrays[case][:, method].mean() for case in ['A', 'C', 'D']]\n        deviation = [arrays[case][:, method].mean(axis=1).std(ddof=1) for case in ['A', 'C', 'D']]\n        axis.errorbar(np.arange(3) + offset, means, yerr=deviation, color=COLORS[method], marker='o', capsize=3, linestyle='none', markersize=5, label=METHODS[method])\n    axis.set(xticks=range(3), xticklabels=['Intact', 'Constant', 'Column-shifted'], ylabel='Sealed-target MAE', ylim=(.025, .082))\n    axis.grid(axis='y', alpha=.16)\n    figure.legend(loc='lower center', ncol=3, frameon=False, columnspacing=.7, handletextpad=.3)\n    figure.subplots_adjust(left=.14, right=.98, bottom=.30, top=.95)\n    save_plot(figure, 'history_structure_controls')\n    create_overview_placeholder()\n    create_manifest()\n\n\ndef resample_bounds(episodes):\n    \"\"\"@evidence[[source_evidence/evaluate_final.py#L999-L1017]]\"\"\"\n    groups = sorted({group for episode in episodes for case in ['A', 'B'] for group in episode['solution']['cases'][case]['resampling_components']})\n    group_index = {group: index for index, group in enumerate(groups)}\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(424242)\n    samples = np.zeros((400, 5))\n    for resample in range(len(samples)):\n        multiplicity = np.bincount(rng.integers(len(groups), size=len(groups)), minlength=len(groups))\n        for episode in episodes:\n            for case in ['A', 'B']:\n                condition = episode['solution']['cases'][case]\n                weights = np.asarray([multiplicity[group_index[group]] for group in condition['resampling_components']], dtype=float)\n                if weights.sum() == 0:\n                    samples[resample] -= np.ones(5) / (2 * len(episodes))\n                else:\n                    gains = np.asarray(condition['baseline_mae_by_method_row_checkpoint']).mean(axis=2) - np.asarray(condition['mae_by_row_checkpoint']).mean(axis=1)\n                    samples[resample] += gains @ weights / weights.sum() / (2 * len(episodes))\n    return np.quantile(samples, [.005, .995], axis=0)\n\n\ndef create_tables(summary):\n    evidence = '% @evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes]]\\n'\n    lines = [evidence, r'\\begin{tabular}{lrrr}', r'\\toprule', r'Estimator & Model holdout & Family holdout & Overall \\\\', r'\\midrule']\n    for index, method in enumerate(METHODS):\n        means = [summary['cases'][case]['mean'][index] for case in ['A', 'B']] + [summary['primary_mean'][index]]\n        lines.append(method + ' & ' + ' & '.join(f'{value:.5f}' for value in means) + r' \\\\')\n    lines.extend([r'\\bottomrule', r'\\end{tabular}'])\n    Path('tables/main_comparison.tex').write_text('\\n'.join(lines) + '\\n')\n    lines = [evidence, r'\\begin{tabular}{llrrrr}', r'\\toprule', r'Holdout & Estimator & $k=1$ & $k=2$ & $k=4$ & $k=8$ \\\\', r'\\midrule']\n    for case, label in [('A', 'Model'), ('B', 'Family')]:\n        for index, method in enumerate(METHODS):\n            values = summary['cases'][case]['mean_budget'][index]\n            lines.append(label + ' & ' + method + ' & ' + ' & '.join(f'{value:.5f}' for value in values) + r' \\\\')\n        if case == 'A':\n            lines.append(r'\\midrule')\n    lines.extend([r'\\bottomrule', r'\\end{tabular}'])\n    Path('tables/budget_details.tex').write_text('\\n'.join(lines) + '\\n')\n    lines = [evidence, r'\\begin{tabular}{lrrrrrr}', r'\\toprule', r'Seed & Col. mean & Query mean & Random LR & Var. LR & Ridge & Studied \\\\', r'\\midrule']\n    for seed, values in zip(summary['seeds'], summary['primary_seed']):\n        lines.append(str(seed) + ' & ' + ' & '.join(f'{value:.5f}' for value in values) + r' \\\\')\n    lines.append(r'\\midrule')\n    lines.append('Seed SD & ' + ' & '.join(f'{value:.5f}' for value in summary['primary_seed_sd']) + r' \\\\')\n    lines.extend([r'\\bottomrule', r'\\end{tabular}'])\n    Path('tables/seed_details.tex').write_text('\\n'.join(lines) + '\\n')\n    for path in Path('tables').glob('*.tex'):\n        provenance(path, 'table')\n\n\ndef create_overview_placeholder():\n    if Path('.concept_figure_complete').exists():\n        return\n    prompt_path = Path('figures/method_overview.prompts.json')\n    if prompt_path.exists() and json.loads(prompt_path.read_text()):\n        return\n    image_path = Path('figures/method_overview.png')\n    if not image_path.exists():\n        from PIL import Image, ImageDraw\n        image = Image.new('RGB', (2400, 950), 'white')\n        draw = ImageDraw.Draw(image)\n        draw.text((70, 70), 'Overview reserved for synchronous concept-figure rendering', fill='#555555', font_size=42)\n        image.save(image_path)\n    if not prompt_path.exists():\n        prompt_path.write_text('{}\\n')\n\n\ndef create_manifest():\n    common = dict(placement='full_width', intended_latex_width_fraction=1.0, estimated_min_rendered_font_pt=8.8, font_sizes=dict(title=10, axis=9, ticks=9, legend=9), source_ids=['final.evidence.episodes'], max_label_chars=36, uses_abbrev_labels=True, uses_progression=False)\n    figures = [dict(common, figure_id='method_overview', figure_type='diagram', path_png='figures/method_overview.png', generator='generate-concept-figure', prompt_log_path='figures/method_overview.prompts.json', n_panels=2, panels_per_row=1, categories_per_panel=[5, 5], series_per_panel=[2, 2], source_ids=[]),\n               dict(common, figure_id='budget_comparison', figure_type='line', path_pdf='figures/budget_comparison.pdf', path_png='figures/budget_comparison.png', generator='matplotlib', n_panels=2, panels_per_row=2, categories_per_panel=[4, 4], series_per_panel=[4, 4]),\n               dict(common, figure_id='history_structure_controls', figure_type='scatter', path_pdf='figures/history_structure_controls.pdf', path_png='figures/history_structure_controls.png', generator='matplotlib', n_panels=1, panels_per_row=1, categories_per_panel=[3], series_per_panel=[3], intended_latex_width_fraction=.9)]\n    Path('figure_manifest.json').write_text(json.dumps(dict(figures=figures), indent=2))\n\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    main()\n# Reproduction package\n\n## Scope and status\n\nThis is a retrospective embedding-score prediction study on previously observed\nMTEB task/subset cells. The independent final evaluation completed and qualified.\nIts retained evidence, including unfavorable historical-data controls, is preserved\nin read-only `paper_data.json`. No new model experiment was run while writing the\npaper. The configuration-level comparison does not isolate residual transfer.\n\n## Environment\n\nThe evaluated task declares Python dependencies `numpy==1.26.4` and\n`matplotlib==3.9.2`; Python 3.12 is available in the supplied environment.\nThe numeric artifacts were generated with those declared dependency versions.\nTeX Live, `pdflatex`, `bibtex`, and Poppler `pdftotext` support compilation and\nrendered-text checks. JSON Schema and PDF-layout checks additionally use\n`jsonschema` and PyMuPDF; these validation-only packages need not enter the\nscientific environment. Install environments outside this workspace:\n\n```sh\npython3.12 -m venv /tmp/embedding-paper-env\n/tmp/embedding-paper-env/bin/pip install -r source_evidence/requirements.txt\n/tmp/embedding-paper-env/bin/python build_paper_artifacts.py\npython3 build_claims.py\n```\n\nThe build script only aggregates retained arrays and reproduces the component\nbootstrap. It does not fit or evaluate new models. No timing benchmark of this\nartifact build was collected, so a measured regeneration runtime is unavailable.\nConcept placeholders are self-guarded: the build never overwrites an orchestrator-\ncompleted overview. Final concept rendering is a separate synchronous step.\n\n## Data versions and checking extraction\n\nResults repository: `https://github.com/embeddings-benchmark/results`, revision\n`6dabbcc68c28ea5f180ce7df79347b3ca9cc6383`.\nTask definitions revision: `5a83aafe4e7140d0606b96f59448c704f31dbf76`.\nThe final manifest has 126 rows and 135 task/subset columns. The raw source JSON\ndocuments used to construct each row are embedded in\n`source_evidence/resources/final/rows.jsonl`; definitions, normalization rules,\nresource fingerprints, and split assignments are bundled alongside them.\nThe evaluator's `extract` and `load_resources` functions re-extract scores and\ncheck exact agreement with the stored normalized matrix, source digests, and splits.\nNo network is needed to reconstruct this matrix from the bundled documents.\n\nOptional upstream checkout, not needed for manuscript regeneration:\n\n```sh\ngit clone --filter=blob:none https://github.com/embeddings-benchmark/results /tmp/mteb-results\ngit -C /tmp/mteb-results checkout 6dabbcc68c28ea5f180ce7df79347b3ca9cc6383\n```\n\nThe bundled final plane is the authoritative reproduction input, not a fresh\nselection from a current leaderboard. The original upstream subset-construction\nutility is not present; the final extraction/checking code and all selected raw\ndocuments are present. The manifest records current CC0-1.0 results-license evidence,\nApache-2.0 definitions metadata, and absence of a results license at the pinned\nsnapshot. Do not silently resolve that historical licensing caveat.\n\n## Evaluated source\n\n- `source_evidence/selected/src/program.py`: evaluated predictor, including ALS,\n  acquisition, donor folds, local medians, calibration, reset, and prediction.\n- `source_evidence/selected/program_spec.toml`: unchanged entrypoint specification.\n- `source_evidence/selected/RESIDUAL_METHOD.md`: accompanying method note.\n- `source_evidence/original/`: supplied original predictor for inspection only;\n  no paired final result for this exact file is asserted.\n- `source_evidence/evaluate_final.py`: complete frozen evaluator and five references.\n- `source_evidence/resources/final/plan.json`: seeds 6841, 8089, 9011 and splits.\n- `source_evidence_manifest.json`: copy fingerprints and original evidence locations.\n\nFor an independent future rerun, outside manuscript-only revision:\n\n```sh\nOMP_NUM_THREADS=1 OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1 MKL_NUM_THREADS=1 \\\n  /tmp/embedding-paper-env/bin/python source_evidence/evaluate_final.py \\\n  --program_path source_evidence/selected/src/program.py \\\n  --results_dir /tmp/embedding-final-rerun\n```\n\nThis command was not run during paper writing. It fits models and changes no\nsealed registry entries. The evaluator imposes its own CPU/thread, resource,\nmessage, and 7200-second wall-time limits. Recorded seed durations, including\ntheir primary and disruption conditions but excluding reset replay, were\n77.4804, 63.8990, and 61.9266 seconds. These are retained measurements, not\nruntime guarantees for another environment.\n<!-- @evidence[[paper_data.json#/final_evaluation/evaluation_evidence/episodes]] -->\n\n## Tables, figures, and claims\n\nAll numeric outputs come from `build_paper_artifacts.py`:\n\n| Manuscript object | Output |\n| --- | --- |\n| Main comparison table | `tables/main_comparison.tex` |\n| Supplementary budget table | `tables/budget_details.tex` |\n| Supplementary seed table | `tables/seed_details.tex` |\n| Figure 2: holdout/budget comparison | `figures/budget_comparison.pdf` and `.png` |\n| Figure 3: history controls | `figures/history_structure_controls.pdf` and `.png` |\n| All derived statistics and bootstrap bounds | `derived_results.json` |\n\nSupplementary tables are embedded verbatim in `paper.tex` to satisfy source-only\nsupplement validation; their generated versions above must agree exactly.\nThe settings table is a transcription of the source configuration, not an\nadditional experiment. Figure 1 is qualitative, rendered from the strategy and\nmanuscript by the separate concept-figure workflow; its prompt log accompanies it.\nThe writing-stage PNG is explicitly a reserved placeholder until that renderer\ncompletes. Do not treat its presence as completed visual production.\n`figure_manifest.json` records paths, generators, density, and final-layout sizes.\nEvery quantitative plot has vector PDF and 300-DPI PNG exports.\n`build_claims.py` writes `claims_grounding.json`, combining registry source IDs\nwith readable source locations; hashes alone never support method semantics.\n\n## References and restrictions\n\n`retrieve_paper_references.py` retrieves exactly identified classical references\nand explicitly permitted starter papers. Semantic Scholar rate limits prompted\nOpenAlex fallback. Consulted abstracts and metadata are retained under\n`literature_evidence/`; no citation network was followed. One incorrect DOI was\nrejected rather than cited. Publisher metadata from the original JMLR article\ncorrects malformed concatenated author names in its OpenAlex record; the permitted\nstarter title corrects the `Langauge` spelling error in another record. No\nencounter with the prohibited study was identified. This is not an exhaustive\nliterature survey or a novelty/priority verification.\n\n## Compilation and validation\n\nThe manuscript uses the official ICLR 2026 review template, fetched from\n`ICLR/Master-Template/iclr2026`; exact URLs and repository file identities are in\n`template_provenance.json`. No author identities, acknowledgements, or funding\nstatements are inserted. The separate LLM Usage disclosure appears in the supplement.\n\n```sh\npython3 .codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_tex_refs.py --tex paper.tex --bib references.bib\npython3 .codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/scripts/validate_claims.py \\\n  --paper-data paper_data.json --references references_provenance.json \\\n  --bib references.bib --claims claims_grounding.json --paper-dir .\nbash .codex/skills/scientific-evidence/scripts/scientific_evidence.sh verify --root-dir .\nbash .codex/skills/validate-paper/scripts/compile_latex.sh paper.tex\n```\n\nIf the environment-specific canonical compile-input gate rejects Debian's\nsystem configuration symlink, `sh compile_paper_locally.sh` runs direct\n`pdflatex`, `bibtex`, and two more `pdflatex` passes for diagnosis; this does not\nmean that the canonical input gate passed. `local_validation_report.json` records actual checks and any unavailable\ncanonical checks. Quantitative source links and adjacent provenance sidecars are\nchecked by `scientific-evidence/verification-report.json`.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
